From 23d6c06a9cbb7a6fcd77655292e1cf2750cc6ea7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azra Bano <azrabano.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:02:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Bracket the linesearch at constraint zone boundaries.

The linesearch cost is piecewise smooth: its curvature jumps where a
constraint changes zone, e.g. where an elliptic contact crosses the cone
boundary, by up to a factor of about impratio. Newton steps from the bracket
ends use the curvature on their own side of such a boundary and overshoot
across it, so the bracketed search degenerated to bisection at three
evaluations per halving. With elliptic cones, impratio=10 and
ls_iterations=20 it could exhaust its budget without improvement and end the
solve at a non-minimizer, a fixed point of restarting from its own qacc
(#3628).

In the bracketed phase, evaluate at the zone boundary nearest to the
bracket midpoint, when the bracket contains one, instead of at the midpoint.
Boundaries are computed in closed form per constraint: the zero crossing of
inequalities, the friction loss bounds, and the roots of the two elliptic
cone boundary quadratics. Also skip evaluating Newton candidates that fall
outside the bracket: the derivative is monotone, so they cannot improve on
the bracket ends.
